{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790345143,"nonce":"Eyh+1qyCgmNfcb0JDytKVWiJ4uE=","message":"Design (2026-09-25, workflow zypy-asyncio-design; three readers, a designer and a skeptic who checked every citation against main 795c9ecf and every claim against CPython 3.14; the skeptic's corrections are applied below).\n\nPrinciple. asyncio in zypy is Python's surface over Zyntax's own async machinery, split the way CPython itself splits it. A Python coroutine is a krio async state machine: the entry plus `{name}$poll`, built by apply_krio_async_lowering (crates/zyntax_embed/src/krio_lowering.rs:271-510). `await` is Intrinsic::Await (crates/compiler/src/hir.rs:2466). A Task is an executor task whose root is that machine. A Future is a runtime record that settles once and wakes the tasks parked on it. The event loop is the Zyntax executor (today drive_until, crates/zyntax_embed/src/runtime/promise.rs:683-801), grown into CPython's BaseEventLoop scheduling model: one FIFO ready queue of handles, a timer heap and a thread-safe wake inbox.\n\n**Which parts are native.** The core types are native, as they are in CPython, where Future, Task, the running-loop state and current_task live in the C module `_asyncio` and contexts in `_contextvars`. That covers the coroutine object, Future, Task, the loop, Handle and TimerHandle, current_task and the running loop, sleep, contextvars, and the async-generator object. The policy layers are CPython 3.14's own Lib/asyncio sources, compiled by zypy against those native types, so their semantics hold by construction: exceptions, locks, queues, timeouts, taskgroups, gather/wait/wait_for/shield/as_completed in tasks.py, runners, coroutines and events. They are bundled the way decimal.py already is (crates/zyntax_python/src/modules.rs:21-26).\n\n**What gets added, and where.** Every gap is built as a language-neutral capability of krio_adapter and zyntax_embed:\n- a status-only poll ABI with an outcome slot\n- a poll context `cx` that carries the task, the park target and an injected exception\n- a wake that re-polls the root task\n- exception injection at the suspension point\n- a thread-safe inbox with a host notifier\n- task-local words\n- a GC root provider for suspended machines\n- an async role kept in HIR\n\nA frontend contributes only hooks of the shape it already has. zb_hook_raise is declared by the library and defined by the frontend (crates/zyntax_builtins/src/lib.rs:51-56, 286-292; crates/zyntax_python/src/classes.rs:2621-2690). Nothing is emulated. A Python-level `send()`-driven Task is not compiled, and no generator trampoline sits under coroutines.\n\nBoth embedder requirements from e9086df fall out of the same core:\n- (1) A foreign awaitable is a runtime Future that the embedder settles through a Send `Settler`. The settle goes through the inbox, so from Python's view it is `call_soon_threadsafe(fut.set_result, v)`.\n- (2) An exported async def is a Task root. The host drives it through a coroutine token modelled on the fiber token API (crates/zyntax_embed/src/runtime/tiered.rs:1824-1965), and the token reports Pending, Ready(value), Raised(exception) or Cancelled.\n\nEvidence: no code was changed, built or run. Every claim is from reading main at a900deba. The executor defects listed in gaps are inferred from the code and still need a test to confirm.\n\nMapping (Python construct: Zyntax primitive [status]):\n- Embedder req (1): `await f` on a foreign object, settled from any thread: The nearest existing shape is the host-bridge park: `__zyntax_async_*` symbols are rewritten into register_future + bridge(handle) + return Pending (crates/passes/krio_adapter/src/abi_emit.rs:486-509, 818, 942-1150), and settled by resolve_future (crates/zyntax_embed/src/host_futures.rs:501-572). The Foreign trait (crates/zyntax_embed/src/foreign.rs:51-83) is synchronous and has no await notion. [gap] Gap: Foreign::poll_await/cancel_await, Settler, the thread-safe inbox and the executor Future. Every table today is thread_local (host_futures.rs:134-167, 255), so a cross-thread resolve_future returns UnknownHandle (host_futures.rs:531-534).\n- Embedder req (2): an exported async def driven by the host; its value or exception read back: call_async returns a ZyntaxPromise (crates/zyntax_embed/src/runtime/tiered.rs:889) that decodes every ready value as Int (promise.rs:261-310). The fiber token API is the model to mirror: get_fiber/resume_fiber_within/drop_fiber, with the yield shape recorded in fiber_shapes (tiered.rs:122-126, 1824-1965). [gap] Gap: The token API; typed decoding of the result; the Raised and Cancelled steps. The async-ness also has to stay visible after krio: see the next row.\n- TypedFunction.is_async visible to the embedder in the typed AST and HIR: TypedFunction.is_async (crates/typed_ast/src/typed_ast.rs:399) is copied to HirFunctionSignature.is_async (crates/compiler/src/hir.rs:341; lowering.rs:4054). krio clears it on the poll fn and on the entry (abi_emit.rs:2244, 2323), so ZyntaxRuntime.async_functions is empty on the krio path (crates/zyntax_embed/src/runtime/classic.rs:281-289). [exists-needs-surface] Gap: AsyncRole in HIR; async_shapes; classic.rs:281-289 reads the role.\n- async def: krio async lowering, run per function with is_async: orchestrator::lower_async_function (crates/passes/krio_adapter/src/orchestrator.rs:153-374), reshape_to_poll_abi (abi_emit.rs:1972-2257), generate_promise_entry (abi_emit.rs:2292-2552). zypy refuses it (crates/zyntax_python/src/lower.rs:1896-1897). [gap] Gap: Async methods work through TypedMethod.is_async (typed_ast.rs:1817). Two things are missing. First, async lambdas and closures: TypedLambda has no is_async (typed_ast.rs:1043-1047). Second, a nested async def that captures needs a heap environment, because closure environments are stack slots and would dangle once the creating frame returns.\n- await \u003ccoroutine call\u003e: Intrinsic::Await (hir.rs:2466), lowered in SSA (crates/compiler/src/ssa.rs:7159-7310) and then by the generic poll-through path (abi_emit.rs:394-815). [exists-needs-surface] Gap: The ready-block fall-through; freeing the child at Ready; the Raised status at the await site (see the Exceptions field).\n- await \u003cany other value\u003e (a stored coroutine, Task, Future, foreign object, or an object with __await__): The non-call Await form treats the value as a {sm, poll_fn} pointer (ssa.rs:7292-7310; abi_emit.rs:540-620). This would crash on a boxed dynamic value. [gap] Gap: The adapter, the COROUTINE box tag and the frontend __await__ hook.\n- Coroutine object: created unstarted, awaited once, 'never awaited' warning, close/send/throw, cr_running: The promise {sm@0, poll_fn@8} (abi_emit.rs:2300-2313). There is no terminal state: polling a finished machine re-enters its last state (dispatcher at crates/passes/krio_adapter/src/emit.rs:568-630, default at :606). [exists-needs-surface] Gap: The header flags, the DONE state and the Reused status. The warning's timing depends on release timing: CPython's refcount finalization is immediate, while zypy leaves unproven releases to the collector (crates/zyntax_python/src/lib.rs:245-249).\n- Poll result: value, None, exception: Today a single i64: 0 means Pending, a void return is 1, and a value is cast to i64 (abi_emit.rs:2150-2230, 2258-2268). ZyntaxPromise reads a negative value as Failed and anything else as Int (promise.rs:261-310). The timer path reads a negative value as Ready (host_futures.rs:545-563). [gap] Gap: This changes reshape_to_poll_abi step 6, every await site, promise.rs and the plugin SDK together.\n- asyncio.Future (create_future, set_result, set_exception, cancel, result, exception, add/remove_done_callback, done, cancelled, get_loop): The nearest pieces are ParkedFuture (host_futures.rs:66-88) and ZyntaxPromise (promise.rs:43). Neither is a value that settles once and wakes its waiters. [gap] Gap: The Future record and callbacks; zypy classes subclassing a native base (d3acf39).\n- asyncio.Task, create_task, current_task, all_tasks, Task.get_coro/get_name/set_name, eager_start: Tasks today are a host-supplied slice whose id is the slice index (promise.rs:683-801, 697). Codegen passes task_id 0 (abi_emit.rs:963-968) and __zyntax_register_future substitutes CURRENT_TASK_ID (host_futures.rs:167-177, 695-722). Compiled code has no spawn. [gap] Gap: The executor task slab and spawn ABI. This also fixes await_with_timeout deregistering task 0 (promise.rs:516) and the id collisions between separate drives.\n- The event loop object (time, call_soon, call_later, call_at, call_soon_threadsafe, run_until_complete, run_forever, stop, close, exception handler, task factory, debug): drive_until (promise.rs:683-801) and TIMER_QUEUE (host_futures.rs:246-330). There is no ready queue: the only wake sources are timers and re-polling roots. [gap] Gap: The ready queue, the heapq-ordered timer heap, the inbox and host mode.\n- asyncio.sleep(delay, result): `sleep` is a builtins alias to __zyntax_async_set_timeout, which only schedules a timer (crates/zyntax_embed/src/effect_runtime.rs:968-980). [gap] Gap: The yield-now leaf; the timer as a Future (see the executor defects under gaps).\n- gather(return_exceptions), wait(FIRST_COMPLETED/FIRST_EXCEPTION/ALL_COMPLETED), wait_for, shield, as_completed, ensure_future: The host-only combinators PromiseAll, PromiseRace and PromiseAllSettled (promise.rs:874-1300) poll a fixed slice and are not reachable from compiled code. [gap] Gap: zypy prerequisites: *args (refused at lower.rs:1899-1900), decorators (lower.rs:1893-1895), native-base subclassing and callbacks as values.\n- asyncio.timeout / timeout_at / Timeout.reschedule (3.11+): None; await_with_timeout is host-only (promise.rs:507-535). [gap] Gap: async with; enum (_State); the native Task cancel bookkeeping.\n- Event, Lock, Semaphore, BoundedSemaphore, Condition, Barrier, Queue, PriorityQueue, LifoQueue, QueueShutDown (3.13): None in Zyntax. They are pure policy over futures. [gap] Gap: collections.deque, heapq, async with (__aenter__/__aexit__) and native-base classes in zypy.\n- TaskGroup (3.11+): None. [gap] Gap: ExceptionGroup/BaseExceptionGroup in the zypy prelude (crates/zyntax_python/src/prelude.rs:25-32 defines BaseException and Exception); except*, which try_stmt refuses (crates/zyntax_python/src/lower.rs:9734-9736); async with.\n- Cancellation: Task.cancel(msg), CancelledError at the suspension point, uncancel, cancelling, shield: FiberCancel only makes the next resume report Done (crates/passes/krio_adapter/src/fiber.rs:328-331). Task cancel is teardown without resuming (host_futures.rs:424-446). There is no injection. [gap] Gap: cx.inject, and the leaf and state-0 checks that consume it.\n- Exceptions across await, task exception storage, 'Task exception was never retrieved': zypy keeps the in-flight exception in the global py$exc (crates/zyntax_python/src/lower.rs:1065-1066) and checks it after fallible calls (pending_check, lower.rs:1455-1475). The library hook zb_hook_raise is defined by the frontend (classes.rs:2621-2690). There is no error channel on the async rail: reject resolves -1 (host_futures.rs:633-638). [gap] Gap: ExceptionAbi hooks used by krio, and py$exc made a task-local word.\n- contextvars (ContextVar, Token, copy_context, Context.run); a Task's context; callback contexts: Per-task handler segments already bracket every task poll (effect_runtime.rs:529-545; promise.rs:694-700). This proves the save/restore point exists. [gap] Gap: Task-local words and a native _contextvars module.\n- get_running_loop, _get_running_loop, get_event_loop (3.14 raises when there is no current loop), set_event_loop, new_event_loop: CURRENT_TASK_ID is a thread-local (host_futures.rs:167-177). There is no loop object. [gap] Gap: The loop object.\n- Async generators: __anext__, asend, athrow, aclose, StopAsyncIteration, sys.set_asyncgen_hooks, loop.shutdown_asyncgens: async and fiber are exclusive on one function (hir.rs:341-347), and await is refused inside a fiber (ssa.rs:7159-7178). krio already numbers Await and PerformEffect suspensions as DirectYield in one table (crates/passes/krio_adapter/src/lib.rs:704-730). [gap] Gap: A YieldValue suspension kind and the Yielded status.\n- async for, async comprehensions: Refused in zypy (lower.rs:4916-4917). [gap] Gap: The frontend lowering.\n- async with: Refused in zypy (crates/zyntax_python/src/bytes.rs:125-133). General `with` is also uncovered (git-bug 70ab640, item 4). [gap] Gap: The context-manager protocol in zypy, which comes first.\n- A sync generator iterated inside a coroutine: zypy generators are fibers (lower.rs:238, 2015-2038). A fiber driven inside an async fn keeps its handle across awaits (crates/zynml/tests/fiber_in_async.rs). [exists-needs-surface] Gap: None.\n- Generator-based awaitables (__await__ returning an iterator, @types.coroutine): Fibers (lower.rs:238), stepped inside a poll (fiber_in_async.rs). [exists-needs-surface] Gap: Generator return value and throw (git-bug 4f32f29, item 1); the __await__ hook in the adapter.\n- asyncio.run / Runner (3.11+), including loop_factory: The host side has call_async + await_raw only (promise.rs:422-445). The zypy CLI calls main synchronously (crates/zyntax_python/src/main.rs:120-125 builds the TieredRuntime). [gap] Gap: Native minimal signal and threading.current_thread; functools.partial.\n- Suspended coroutines under the collector: Roots are the stacks, globals and the fiber provider (crates/compiler/src/collector.rs:1686-1697; krio_adapter/src/fiber.rs:333-386). SM slot arrays come from the pool, and while parked they are referenced only from Rust tables. [gap] Gap: The provider hook in the collector.\n- loop.run_in_executor, asyncio.to_thread, sockets, streams, subprocess, add_reader/add_writer: None. The collector turns itself off when a second thread uses the pool (collector.rs:365-393). [gap] Gap: An I/O poller wake source; a thread-safe Python runtime for to_thread.\n- Hot coroutines tiering to LLVM: Cranelift lowers AsyncSaveSlot and AsyncLoadSlot (cranelift_backend.rs:6545-6620). LLVM has no arm and falls into \"Instruction not yet implemented\" (crates/compiler/src/llvm_backend.rs:3777-3782), so an LLVM failure leaves the function on Cranelift (tiered_backend.rs:4425-4436). [gap] Gap: The LLVM arms.\n\nLanguage-neutral runtime work (Zyntax, not zypy):\n- The poll ABI conflates value and status. A poll should return only a status (Pending 0, Ready 1, Raised 2, Yielded 3, Reused 4) and keep the value in a fixed outcome slot. Today 0 means Pending, so a None, 0 or False result reads as Pending forever, and a negative result reads as Failed on one path (crates/zyntax_embed/src/runtime/promise.rs:261-310) and as Ready on the other (crates/zyntax_embed/src/host_futures.rs:545-563). Change reshape_to_poll_abi step 6 (crates/passes/krio_adapter/src/abi_emit.rs:2150-2230), every await site, ZyntaxPromise, and ZrtlPromise with a version bump (sdk/zrtl/src/async_support.rs:133-197).\n- A poll context parameter `cx` (task, parked_on, inject, yield_now), passed down the poll-through chain. It replaces the CURRENT_TASK_ID substitution and codegen's constant task_id 0 (abi_emit.rs:963-968; host_futures.rs:167-177, 695-722). On wasm the poll signature has to match exactly, because call_indirect traps on a mismatch.\n- The await_ready block returns Pending after its child completes (abi_emit.rs:575-584, 693-713). It must branch into the resume block. Without that, a task whose child finishes synchronously takes a spurious loop turn, and under a real waker it would never be re-polled.\n- There is no terminal state: polling a finished SM re-runs its tail (dispatcher default at crates/passes/krio_adapter/src/emit.rs:606). Add a DONE state that returns Reused, plus coroutine header flags (CREATED, RUNNING, SUSPENDED, CLOSED, awaited_by).\n- Wake the root task, not the leaf. resolve_future polls the leaf SM in place and reports its value as the task's (host_futures.rs:530-572; promise.rs:756-765). Host bridges must instead await a runtime Future through the generic path, so the state does not advance before the settle. Today it advances first (abi_emit.rs:1087-1095).\n- Executor: a runtime Future record with done callbacks; a slab of tasks with stable, generational ids; a dynamic ready queue of handles; a timer heap with heapq's tie order and CPython's compaction; a compiled-code spawn ABI (__zyntax_task_spawn, __zyntax_current_task, __zyntax_call_soon/_at, __zyntax_future_new/_settle, __zyntax_yield_now). This replaces drive_until's slice indices (promise.rs:683-801) and await_with_timeout's hard-coded deregister of task 0 (promise.rs:516).\n- Exception injection at the suspension point. cx.inject is consumed by the first suspension point that resumes: a leaf awaitable, a YieldValue site, or the state-0 prologue in emit_dispatcher (emit.rs:568-630). It serves Task.cancel's must_cancel path, coroutine.throw/close and async-generator athrow/aclose, without unwinding JIT frames.\n- An ExceptionAbi (raise_kind, which is the existing zb_hook_raise at crates/zyntax_builtins/src/lib.rs:286-292, plus take_pending and set_pending) that krio uses at coroutine exits and await sites. Without it, a Raised child propagates automatically.\n- A thread-safe inbox (Mutex\u003cVecDeque\u003e, an AtomicBool, and a condvar or eventfd), a host notifier (Waker) and a TimerHook; the Send Settler whose thunk runs on the loop thread; Foreign::poll_await and cancel_await (crates/zyntax_embed/src/foreign.rs:51-83). Every table today is thread_local (host_futures.rs:134-167, 255).\n- Task-local words: module globals the executor saves and restores per handle, placed at the existing task_handler_enter/leave point (crates/zyntax_embed/src/effect_runtime.rs:529-545). zypy registers py$exc (crates/zyntax_python/src/lower.rs:1065-1066) and the current contextvars Context.\n- An async GC root provider. Live SM regions and Future record words must be reported to the collector the way the fiber backend reports stacks and held words (crates/compiler/src/collector.rs:1686-1697; crates/passes/krio_adapter/src/fiber.rs:333-386). zypy runs MarkSweep (crates/zyntax_python/src/lib.rs:249).\n- The async role in HIR. krio clears is_async on the entry and on $poll (abi_emit.rs:2244, 2323). Replace that with AsyncRole::Entry{poll, result} or AsyncRole::Poll, and record async_shapes before lowering the way fiber_shapes are (crates/zyntax_embed/src/runtime/tiered.rs:122-126). ZyntaxRuntime.async_functions then works (crates/zyntax_embed/src/runtime/classic.rs:281-289).\n- A host coroutine token API: start_coroutine, poll_coroutine, cancel_coroutine and drop, returning CoroutineStep {Pending, Ready(typed), Raised(exception), Cancelled}, plus a !Send impl Future. It replaces the Int-only ZyntaxPromise decoding and the Future impl that never wakes (promise.rs:1309-1331).\n- Type::Coroutine(T) in the typed AST, next to Type::Fiber (crates/typed_ast/src/type_registry.rs:430). Today an async call is typed T (crates/typed_ast/src/type_checker.rs:765-769) and await gets a fresh type variable (type_checker.rs:1401-1405).\n- An async-generator SM kind: a YieldValue suspension, the Yielded status and a send slot, added to krio's DirectYield classification (crates/passes/krio_adapter/src/lib.rs:704-730).\n- Async lambdas and closures: TypedLambda has no is_async (crates/typed_ast/src/typed_ast.rs:1043-1047). A capturing nested async def needs a heap environment, because closure environments are stack slots.\n- LLVM arms for AsyncSaveSlot and AsyncLoadSlot (crates/compiler/src/llvm_backend.rs:3777-3782). The HIR interpreter's arms (crates/compiler/src/hir_interp.rs:2033-2084) must take the new cx parameter.\n- zypy prerequisites for compiling Lib/asyncio: decorators (crates/zyntax_python/src/lower.rs:1893-1895); *args and **kwargs (lower.rs:1899-1900); classes with inheritance from native bases, properties and classmethods (git-bug d3acf39); with and async with (git-bug 70ab640 item 4; crates/zyntax_python/src/bytes.rs:125-133); except* and ExceptionGroup (lower.rs:9734-9736); `from x import *` with __all__; enum, collections.deque, heapq, functools.partial, warnings, types.GenericAlias and sys.set_asyncgen_hooks (git-bug 49a1570); generator return value, send and throw (git-bug 4f32f29).\n- Release timing for the finalizer messages: \"coroutine was never awaited\", \"Task exception was never retrieved\", \"Task was destroyed but it is pending!\" and the async-generator finalizer. CPython emits them at refcount zero. zypy releases only what it proves dead and leaves the rest to the collector (crates/zyntax_python/src/lib.rs:245-249), so these come at a later collection or at loop close.\n- Call-graph introspection added in 3.14 (asyncio.graph, future_add_to_awaited_by) needs awaiter links from each task to the Futures and tasks it awaits. It comes after the core.\n- Suspected executor defects, derived from the code and not yet run, to be pinned by tests before the rewrite:\n(a) A nested await whose innermost coroutine parks on a timer completes the top-level task with the inner value (promise.rs:756-765; host_futures.rs:344-358).\n(b) A bridge await is skipped by any poll before its settle (abi_emit.rs:1087-1095; promise.rs:786-800).\n(c) A result that encodes as 0 stays Pending forever.\n(d) await_with_timeout deregisters task 0 (promise.rs:516).\n(e) The Future impl is woken only by cancel (promise.rs:483-491, 1309-1331).\n(f) A cross-thread resolve_future returns UnknownHandle.\nThe probe file is at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-amaterasu-Vibranium-zyntax/56183c5f-5acc-4cc6-9954-39174de9c11a/scratchpad/asyncio_probe.rs.\n\nPhases:\n- Phase 0, pin the current behaviour. Run the saved probe (asyncio_probe.rs) in a scratch worktree, on Cranelift, the interpreter and wasm, for defects (a) to (f). File each confirmed defect in git-bug (area:async or the existing runtime area; kind bug), linked to e9086df. These cases become the regression tests for Phases 1 and 2.\n- Phase 1, the runtime ABI, language-neutral. In krio_adapter, zyntax_embed and the SDK:\n- a status-only poll with an outcome slot, and the cx parameter\n- the await_ready fall-through, and freeing the child at Ready\n- the DONE state and the coroutine header flags\n- ExceptionAbi hooks at coroutine exits and await sites\n- AsyncRole in HIR and async_shapes\n- Type::Coroutine\n- the ZrtlPromise ABI bump\nMigrate ZynML's async tests (cooperative_executor, async_effect_composition, fiber_in_async, async_sm_leak, hot_reload_async) and keep them green on Cranelift, the interpreter and wasm.\n- Phase 2, the executor core. Loop with the ready queue, the heapq-ordered timer heap and _run_once replicated; the task slab and spawn ABI; the Future record with done callbacks; root wake; cx.inject; task-local words; the async GC root provider. Timer and host bridges become Futures. drive_until, await_raw, drive_tasks and PromiseAll/Race/AllSettled become wrappers over tasks. The host coroutine token API and CoroutineHandle (impl Future) satisfy embedder requirement (2).\n- Phase 3, cross-thread and embedding. The thread-safe inbox, notifier, TimerHook and host mode (Idle(deadline) with a Waker); Settler; Foreign::poll_await and cancel_await. Grow the stand-in embedder in crates/zyntax_python/tests/foreign.rs with two things: an awaitable settled from another thread while the loop runs other tasks (embedder requirement 1), and an exported async def driven from a Rust future that reads Ready, Raised and Cancelled (embedder requirement 2).\n- Phase 4, zypy async def and await on the native core:\n- lift the async def and await refusals (crates/zyntax_python/src/lower.rs:1896-1897; crates/zyntax_python/src/types.rs:6198)\n- Ty::Coro and the dynamic awaitable adapter\n- zypy's ExceptionAbi (take_pending, set_pending) and py$exc as a task-local word\n- CancelledError under BaseException\n- a native `_asyncio`: Future, Task, the loop, Handle and TimerHandle, current_task, the running loop, sleep, create_task\n- a native `_contextvars`\n- a native asyncio.run shim until runners.py compiles\nConformance cases compare output against CPython 3.14.\n- Phase 5, compile CPython 3.14 Lib/asyncio policy modules as zypy prerequisites land, bundled through modules.rs: exceptions, coroutines, events (policy parts), mixins, locks, queues, timeouts, tasks (gather/wait/wait_for/shield/as_completed/ensure_future), taskgroups (with ExceptionGroup and except*) and runners. Retire the shims. Conformance runs the asyncio test idioms: ordering, return_exceptions, uncancel, shield and timeout conversion.\n- Phase 6, async iteration and context managers. The async-generator SM kind and object with asend, athrow and aclose; the asyncgen hooks and shutdown_asyncgens; async for (static fast path plus the dynamic protocol) and async comprehensions; async with, once sync with lands; generator-based awaitables once generator send and throw land.\n- Phase 7, performance. LLVM arms for the async slot ops; one allocation per coroutine; embedding child SMs; typed unboxed slots. Benchmark pyperformance coroutines, async_tree (none, eager, memoization, cpu_io_mixed) and async_generators, plus a cross-thread settle loop, against CPython 3.14 and PyPy on the Mac and the NUC.\n- Phase 8, later scope. A kqueue or epoll poller as a wake source, with selector_events and streams compiled over native socket and select; run_coroutine_threadsafe and wrap_future on the inbox; 3.14 call-graph introspection; to_thread only once the runtime and collector admit a second mutator thread.\n\nSkeptic: The architecture holds up: CPython's Task/Future algorithm running natively over krio state machines, with a status-plus-outcome-slot poll ABI, root-task wake, cx.inject, a thread-safe inbox and a host token. Most code citations check out: lower_await_calls' ready block returns Pending (abi_emit.rs:577-590, 698-713); a host-bridge await saves next_state before the bridge call; is_async is cleared at abi_emit.rs:2244 and 2323; every async table is thread_local; resolve_future polls the leaf and reports its value to the task; LLVM has no AsyncSaveSlot/AsyncLoadSlot arm; the zypy refusals are at the cited lines. The CPython 3.14 claims are also mostly right: the _run_once order, the uncancel/must_cancel rule, timeout conversion, TaskGroup abort, the Runner.close sequence and gather's context copies. Corrections needed: (1) Line ranges are wrong for drive_until and the sleep/spin citations, and 'sleep' is an alias the embedder configures. (2) Several statuses are overstated: requirement (2), contextvars and sleep are gaps, and async def is not 'only surface work', because zypy's MarkSweep would free parked machines and None/0/False read as Pending. (3) The GC 'provider hook' already exists as add_root_range and WeakHooks. (4) zypy uses neither TypedMethod nor the TypeChecker, so the async-method and Type::Coroutine claims point at ZynML paths. (5) CPython facts to fix: re-entrant send raises ValueError, the loop/Handle/TimerHandle/sleep are Python in CPython, must_cancel is cleared at injection, and 'never retrieved' is not printed at loop close. Missing: lower_to_hir as the place AsyncRole must survive; the snapshot library being built without krio; Allocas live across an await; drop_insert running after krio; almost no TieredRuntime async coverage; the !Send handle versus caribou's scheduler; and more asyncio prerequisites (exception chaining, bound methods as values, WeakSet, BaseExceptionGroup.__new__). Phase 0 remains the right first step, and the defect (a) probe needs an outer coroutine that changes the child's value.\nCorrections applied or to apply when implementing:\n- Claim: The drive_until citations: 'drive_until (promise.rs:683-801)', 'drive_until's yield_now spin (promise.rs:786-800) and its sleep-in-place (promise.rs:763-785)', and defect (b)'s 'promise.rs:786-800'. Correction: Cite drive_until as promise.rs:683-784, the spin as promise.rs:767-781, the deadline sleep as promise.rs:750-755 and the timer sleep as host_futures.rs:349-352. For defect (b), the re-poll that skips a bridge await is promise.rs:773-778, which fires only when no timer is pending.\n- Claim: '`sleep` is a builtins alias to __zyntax_async_set_timeout (effect_runtime.rs:968-980)'. Correction: Say that sleep is an alias the embedder configures (config.builtins or builtin_aliases). zypy has no such alias today.\n- Claim: 'async and fiber are exclusive on one function (hir.rs:341-347)'. Correction: State that exclusivity is a ZynML grammar rule, not a HIR invariant. zypy must keep refusing async def containing yield explicitly until Phase 6, and must never mark it is_generator.\n- Claim: 'Async methods work through TypedMethod.is_async (typed_ast.rs:1817)' (the async def row). Correction: For zypy, async methods and async nested defs (lower.rs:12132) go through function_named. They need is_async set on the TypedFunction and the same entry/poll split. TypedMethod.is_async is irrelevant to zypy.\n- Claim: 'async def' row: 'One to one ... The only surface work is lifting the refusal and giving async bodies the parameter handling that sync bodies have.' Correction: Downgrade to gap. Plain async def in zypy needs at least the status/outcome-slot ABI, GC rooting of parked machines, and a check that drop_insert treats AsyncSaveSlot as an escape on krio'd $poll functions.\n- Claim: The GC row: 'The provider hook in the collector' is a gap. Correction: Reuse add_root_range for the task slab and Future arena, or register a hooks entry whose hold/trace names parked SM blocks. Registering WeakHooks also sets CLEARS_DEAD_FRAMES (collector.rs:519), which is a cost to weigh. Only the executor-side enumeration is new.\n- Claim: Embedder requirement (2) status 'exists-needs-surface'; contextvars status 'exists-needs-surface'; asyncio.sleep status 'exists-needs-surface'. Correction: Mark all three 'gap'. Default-to-doubt applies: nothing of the Future-based sleep, the token or _contextvars exists.\n- Claim: 'A sync generator iterated inside a coroutine' status 'exists'. Correction: Mark it 'exists-needs-surface': the runtime supports it, but it is untested from zypy and on TieredRuntime.\n- Claim: Coroutine row: a re-entrant poll maps to \"coroutine ignored GeneratorExit\" / already executing. Correction: Re-entrant send/throw raises ValueError: coroutine already executing. close() on a coroutine that suspends again after GeneratorExit raises RuntimeError: coroutine ignored GeneratorExit.\n- Claim: Principle: the core types are native 'as they are in CPython', a list that covers the loop, Handle and TimerHandle and sleep. The event_loop field says events.py is compiled 'with its Handle, TimerHandle ... taken from `_asyncio`, the way futures.py and tasks.py import the C versions'. Correction: Making the loop, Handle, TimerHandle and sleep native is a design choice, not 'as in CPython'. Compiling events.py with Handle and TimerHandle swapped for native ones means editing CPython's source, so 'semantics hold by construction' holds only for the unmodified modules. Say which files are patched.\n- Claim: Task step: 'Poll the root ... injecting a CancelledError if must_cancel is set', plus Task.cancel steps 1-4, plus the leaf 'append TaskWakeup(cx.task) ... unless it is already there'. Correction: Clear must_cancel when the injection is made. Clear log_traceback in cancel(). Register the wakeup in the task step from cx.parked_on, not in the leaf, so a task-less send() adds no callback. Add the await-on-itself and foreign-loop checks.\n- Claim: exceptions field: the default handler prints 'Task exception was never retrieved' 'when a task with an unretrieved exception is released or the loop closes'. Correction: Emit it only when the task record is freed. If zypy frees at loop close, treat that as a known difference from CPython and say so.\n- Claim: Defect (d): 'await_with_timeout deregisters task 0 (promise.rs:516)' is a defect in itself. Correction: Restate (d) as id collision across drives. A timeout tears down every parked future and timer carrying id 0, including other tasks'.\n- Claim: Typing: Type::Coroutine in the typed AST 'removes two problems', the async call typed T (type_checker.rs:765-769) and the fresh type variable for await (type_checker.rs:1401-1405). Correction: For zypy, the fix goes in types.rs (Ty::Coro) and in how lower.rs types the Await node. The typed_ast Type::Coroutine and TypeChecker change matters only for ZynML. Also replace krio's Void-to-I64 fallback with the recorded result type.\n- Claim: The GC row: 'Roots are the stacks, globals and the fiber provider (collector.rs:1686-1697)'. Correction: List all four root sources, and build the async provider on the existing ones.\n- Claim: Minor range citations: orchestrator::lower_async_function at orchestrator.rs:153-374; the fiber token API at tiered.rs:1824-1965; FiberCancel 'only makes the next resume report Done (fiber.rs:328-331)'; the await refusal at types.rs:6198. Correction: Fix the ranges as above.\n- Claim: Why it should beat CPython: 'CPython allocates a frame and a coroutine object per call ... runs gather, sleep and the locks through Python-level Future callbacks'. 'PyPy's JIT cannot keep a suspended frame virtual across a suspension'. Correction: State one allocation per coroutine in CPython, a C-level Future/Task core, and Python-level gather/sleep/locks. Drop or source the PyPy claim, and let the Phase 7 numbers make the case.\nMissing from the design:\n- Evidence for requirement (2) that the design does not cite: TieredRuntime::lower_to_hir (crates/zyntax_embed/src/runtime/tiered.rs:1619-1634) is documented as the HIR a host reads to publish a module, and it applies krio before returning, so today is_async is already cleared (abi_emit.rs:2244, 2323) in exactly what caribou reads. AsyncRole has to be written there. The row cites only the classic runtime's async_functions (classic.rs:281-289), but zypy and embedders use TieredRuntime, whose call_async (tiered.rs:889-929) does not consult async_functions.\n- Build-time snapshot: zypy's built-in library is lowered in build.rs with zyntax_embed built `default-features = false, features = [\"parse-only\"]` (crates/zyntax_python/Cargo.toml:39), so use_krio_async is false there (crates/zyntax_embed/src/lower.rs:191). Any async code in the snapshot library, such as a library-level _asyncio shim, would be lowered by the legacy transform_async_function (crates/compiler/src/lowering.rs:3440-3446), not krio. The design must keep async code out of the snapshot or turn krio on in the build.\n- Stack storage live across an await: krio saves SSA values into slots, but an Alloca'd pointee is not moved (krio_adapter/src/lib.rs:51-56, 225-245 create Allocas only for its own locals). Any zypy value kept in a stack slot and live across an await dangles after the poll returns Pending. The design mentions only closure environments of nested async defs. It needs a pass that refuses or promotes an Alloca live across a suspension.\n- drop_insert runs after krio (crates/compiler/src/lib.rs:2405-2426, called from compile_module after apply_krio_async_lowering). With zypy's automatic release on, it must treat AsyncSaveSlot as an escape and must not release at the Pending returns krio adds. No test covers this: async_sm_leak.rs tests only SM release.\n- Test coverage on zypy's runtime: of the async tests, only crates/zynml/tests/hot_reload_async.rs runs on TieredRuntime. cooperative_executor, async_effect_composition, fiber_in_async and async_sm_leak run on the classic runtime. Phase 1 should add TieredRuntime runs (interpreter tier first, then Cranelift after promotion), because that is what zypy executes. How an interpreted $poll becomes callable through the transmute in promise.rs:275-287 and host_futures.rs:595-599 is not addressed.\n- Caribou's scheduler may be multi-threaded. A !Send CoroutineHandle cannot be spawned onto a work-stealing executor. Confirm caribou's constraint, or offer a Send proxy handle that posts polls to the loop thread through the same inbox.\n- Phase 4 must refuse async generators (async def with yield) explicitly until Phase 6. Otherwise the existing generator path (is_generator, lower.rs:1905-1906) makes them fibers, and ssa.rs:7169-7178 then rejects the await inside with a ZynML-flavoured error.\n- Compiling Lib/asyncio needs more zypy prerequisites than the list gives: `raise X from Y` and exception chaining (__cause__/__context__, 70ab640 item 2), which timeouts.py uses (`raise TimeoutError from exc_val`, and _insert_timeout_error walks __context__). BaseExceptionGroup.__new__ returning ExceptionGroup when every member is an Exception. Bound methods and classes as values (d3acf39 item 2), used everywhere as callbacks (add_done_callback(self._on_task_done), call_soon(self.__step)). weakref.WeakSet (base_events' _asyncgens, tasks' _scheduled_tasks). The `inspect` and `types` helpers coroutines.py uses. d3acf39 does not mention subclassing a native base: that is a new item, not part of d3acf39.\n- More CPython 3.14 details the native Future and Task must copy exactly: sleep() raises ValueError on a NaN delay (3.13+); set_exception with a StopIteration raises TypeError, and an exception class is instantiated first; Future.result() on a cancelled future re-raises the stored _cancelled_exc once before making a fresh one; create_task's eager_start runs inline only when the loop is running; a reused __anext__/asend awaitable raises RuntimeError ('cannot reuse already awaited ...').\n- Exact sequencing of the inbox: event_loop step 4 says draining runs the thunks and makes their settles into call_soon-style handles, which costs two iterations. The foreign-await text says the drain settles F directly, which costs one. Pick one. CPython's call_soon_threadsafe appends the handle to _ready at call time, so it runs in the next iteration, before timers made due in that iteration.\n- cx on wasm: WASM_POLL_DISPATCH's signature is Fn(i64, *mut u8) -\u003e i64 (host_futures.rs:130), and the JS dispatcher in zyntax_wasm has the same shape. Adding cx changes that ABI and the interpreter's re-entry path as well as call_indirect. List it with the ZrtlPromise bump.\n- Where the executor gets the frontend hooks from Rust: zb_hook_raise is a compiled program symbol (classes.rs:2621-2690). A native Future that raises CancelledError on the loop, not inside compiled code, needs its address from the runtime (function_pointer, tiered.rs:2608) plus a take_pending that reads the py$exc global's address. The ExceptionAbi needs a registration API, not just symbol names.\n- Settled foreign values and GC: while F is pending, the foreign box being awaited and any Any a settle thunk produces before F's callbacks run have to be rooted. These are Future-record words, but the design names only the outcome and callback words.\n- Phase 0 cannot rely on the existing test to confirm defect (a): async_effect_composition.rs:106-126 awaits work() and returns its value unchanged, so reporting the inner value as the task's gives the same 100. The probe needs an outer coroutine that changes the result, e.g. `return (await work()) + 1`.","files":null}]}